# E §3.1 step 1, L §2.4 (STOP-REPORT 1 of T's re-run, pick P37; T's m0/format/joint/folder): reprint of a set
# holding a joint model prints each file's canonical text and the reality's sha256, as the stored record does.
# Since de9d244a moves imported evaluate at its top, and a reprint, which loads the members first, reached moves
# half loaded through walk: REFCORE-NOT-YET (ImportError). 9296e8dd crashed so.
=== options reprint
=== j.tally
model j
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use m = "m" sha256 "2437ba566c390985157be44193a5f9ef5e9435633246ed3401a46cada2aa9dc6"
  note "T, pre-M1 (#97, chunk 4; G3 review, 5815c57, #105, P17): a member folder of one model file and a part"

input y: num

source s "s"
=== m/a.tally
model mm
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input v: num
=== m/b.tally
part pb
  tally 2

source tb "t"

input wb: num
